            <h2>Understanding the Route Geography</h2>
            <p>The journey from Chicago to Bloomington begins at Union Station in downtown Chicago and moves south-southwest across the Illinois prairie. The route follows the historic alignment of the Illinois Central Railroad, passing through Chicago's southern suburbs before entering the open farmland and small towns of central Illinois. </p>
            <p>The journey passes through diverse landscapes: the urban environment of Chicago gives way to suburban development in Summit and Joliet, followed by the small-town character of Dwight and Pontiac. As the train approaches Bloomington-Normal, the scenery reflects the flat prairie landscape that defines this region of Illinois. The route is historically significant as it follows paths traveled by Abraham Lincoln during his legal and political career. </p>
